          "turn_index": 0,
          "type": "turn",
          "question": "I have been diagnosed with high blood pressure.",
          "answer": "High blood pressure, also known as hypertension, is a condition where the force of blood against the walls of the arteries is consistently too high. Most cases of high blood pressure do not have a single identifiable cause. However, several factors can contribute, including age, genetic predisposition, excess body weight, high sodium intake, low potassium intake, physical inactivity, and chronic stress (source: \"Hypertension (high blood pressure)\"). It often does not cause symptoms, which is why it's important to have regular screenings.\n\nFor managing high blood pressure, lifestyle changes are essential. Here are some general recommendations:\n\n1. **Diet:** \n   - Reduce sodium intake, as high sodium can contribute to increased blood pressure. Focus on reading food labels, as much sodium comes from processed and packaged foods.\n   - Increase potassium-rich foods like fruits, vegetables, and dairy, as they may help lower blood pressure (source: \"Diet for high blood pressure\").\n   - Limit alcohol consumption, as it can raise blood pressure. Recommended limits are up to two drinks per day for men and one for women (source: \"Diet for high blood pressure\").\n\n2. **Physical Activity:**\n   - Aim for at least 150 minutes of moderate-intensity aerobic activity weekly, such as brisk walking or cycling. This can help lower blood pressure as effectively as some medications (source: \"Physical activity for high blood pressure\").\n\n3. **Weight Management:**\n   - Maintaining a healthy weight through diet and exercise is crucial, as excess weight can increase blood pressure.\n\nThese changes are part of a broader approach for overall health management and may also be discussed with your healthcare provider for personalized guidance.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
